Package: hexagonrpcd
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 adduser,
 udev,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Daemon to communicate with Qualcomm DSPs
 Qualcomm processors include Digital Signal Processors (DSP) which can be
 accessed from Linux using the FastRPC protocol. This protocol is used to
 serve remote files to the DSPs and to call functions offloaded to them.
 .
 This package contains hexagonrpcd, the daemon that talks to the Context Hub
 Runtime Environment (the DSP program managing sensors) over FastRPC. It is
 the userspace half of the Qualcomm Sensor Core (SSC) stack used by libssc
 and iio-sensor-proxy-ssc on marble.

Package: libhexagonrpc0.4
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Implementation of the FastRPC protocol -- shared library
 Qualcomm processors include Digital Signal Processors (DSP) which can be
 accessed from Linux using the FastRPC protocol.
 .
 This package contains the shared library implementing the FastRPC
 protocol for hexagonrpcd.